<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kale Akte</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Calacte</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kale Akte, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Calacte, was an ancient town on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, at modern Caronia. It was founded around 446 BCE by the Sicel leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ducetius">Ducetius</a> after his return from exile in Corinth. The town survived as a minor Greek and later Roman community and was the birthplace of the Augustan rhetorician Caecilius of Calacte.</p></div>
